{"schema":2,"commit":"12b19ca76f461fff02b125544e4e875c2c9b337c","branch":"main","base_sha":"cc049b52fa48b6675199edf7a7175714f77f3186","message":"feat(git): status segment, Source Control panel, commit, push and pull (G2–G6)\n\nThe IDE talks to git without a terminal. `GitService` stays the only place a\n`git` process is started (argument lists only, resolved PATH,\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0, GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, LC_ALL=C, timeouts, cancellation),\nand `GitController` is a ChangeNotifier that owns the snapshot and never runs a\ncommand itself.\n\n- G2 — a read-only status-bar segment: branch (or short SHA when detached),\n  `● n` changes, `↑ahead ↓behind`, with the repo root, upstream and\n  credential-stripped remotes in the tooltip. Debounced refresh, single-flight,\n  no polling.\n- G3 — the Source Control tab: staged/unstaged lists with status letters,\n  per-row and bulk Stage/Unstage (`git add --`, `git restore --staged` or\n  `git rm --cached` on an unborn branch), empty states, and a status segment\n  that opens the panel.\n- G4 — commit: `git commit -F -` with the message on stdin, an identity form\n  that writes repository-local config only, `Cmd+Enter`, cancel and timeout.\n- G5 — push: `git push` (or `-u \u003cremote\u003e \u003cbranch\u003e` without an upstream), never\n  a forcing flag, with a confirmation dialog naming the stripped URL.\n- G6 — pull: `git pull --ff-only` plus `GitService.fetch`, because `behind` is\n  only as fresh as the remote-tracking refs; one fetch per mount, never on a\n  status-only refresh. After a pull `FileService.reloadTabsFromDisk()` re-reads\n  open tabs through an injectable reader and refuses to overwrite unsaved edits.\n\nTests: 8 new/extended suites (service contracts against recording fakes and\nthrowaway real repositories, plus widget tests for the panel and the segment).\n`flutter analyze` clean; `flutter test` 671 pass / 8 skipped.","totals":{"added_lines":7439,"ai_added_lines":0,"human_added_lines":7439,"deleted_line